    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 21 June 2005, the erection of a roof extension measuring measuring a 3.95m projection, a height of 2.5m and a width of 9.2m, and a hip to gable alteration measuring a perpendicular depth of 3.95m, a height of 2.7m with a width of 5.15, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the extensions do not exceed 50m3 on the roof, or 70m3 of the original dwellinghouse.\r\n"
